<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>FAQ</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker kicker-l">Answers by topic</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal FAQ for Arkansas Property Owners</h1><p class="lede">Straight answers to the questions we hear most, grouped by topic: the basics, costs, deadlines, Arkansas specifics and working with us.</p><div class="row"><a class="btn btn-red" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-w" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section>
<div class="wrap two"><article class="prose"><nav class="jump" aria-label="FAQ topics"><a href="#t-0">Appraisal basics</a><a href="#t-1">Costs and fees</a><a href="#t-2">Timing and deadlines</a><a href="#t-3">Arkansas specifics</a><a href="#t-4">Working with us</a></nav><h2 id="t-0">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A process in most property policies for resolving disagreements over the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers pick an umpire, and two signatures set the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>When is appraisal the right tool?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>When coverage is accepted and the dispute is about scope or price, such as repair versus replacement, missing line items, pricing or depreciation.</p></div></details><details><summary>When is appraisal the wrong tool?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>When the claim is denied outright, when the dispute is whether a cause of loss is covered, or when the gap is too small to justify appraisal costs.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is the award binding?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Generally yes, on the amount of loss for the items submitted, once two of the three panel members sign. Courts can set aside awards in limited situations such as fraud or a panel exceeding its authority.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-1">Costs and fees</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who pays for appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most policies each side pays its own appraiser and shares the umpire’s fee equally.</p></div></details><details><summary>How do appraisers charge?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Hourly, a flat fee or a percentage of the increase over the carrier’s estimate. Ask for the arrangement in writing.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is the first conversation free?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We review the basics of your claim and tell you honestly whether appraisal is likely to help.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-2">Timing and deadlines</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many residential appraisals finish within one to three months. Large or complex claims take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does invoking appraisal pause my policy deadlines?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Don’t assume so. Suit-limitation and replacement-cost deadlines may keep running. Calendar them and ask an attorney about tolling if a deadline is close.</p></div></details><details><summary>How quickly must I name an appraiser?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many policies say within 20 days of a written demand. Read your policy and act quickly.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-3">Arkansas specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurers in Arkansas?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Arkansas Insurance Department. It handles licensing, rate filings and consumer complaints.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Arkansas have a FAIR plan or wind pool?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Arkansas is inland and has no coastal wind pool. Its statutory residual market is the Arkansas Rural Risk Underwriting Association (ARRUA), which provides basic property coverage for qualifying risks in designated rural areas.</p></div></details><details><summary>What does Arkansas law say about insurer delays?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Arkansas has a statute that can add a statutory penalty and attorney’s fees when an insurer fails to pay a covered loss within the required time after demand, and courts recognize bad-faith claims in limited situations. These are legal questions for an Arkansas attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can labor be depreciated in an Arkansas claim?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Arkansas courts have addressed labor depreciation in actual cash value payments, and the rules have developed over time. Ask the carrier how depreciation was calculated and talk to an attorney if it matters to your claim.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are you public adjusters or attorneys?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Neither. We are appraisers and estimators. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal and don’t give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work statewide?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, in all 75 Arkansas counties, from Benton County in the northwest to Chicot County in the southeast.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I send first?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Your declarations page, the carrier’s full estimate, any letters from the carrier, your photos and any contractor estimate.</p></div></details></div></article>
<aside class="aside"><div class="sbox sbox-call"><h2 class="sbox-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>A short call tells you whether appraisal fits your claim, or whether something else would serve you better.</p><a class="sbox-tel" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> +1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-white btn-block" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="sbox"><h2 class="sbox-t">Resources</h2><ul class="sbox-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-process-explained/">Appraisal process<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/faq/" aria-current="page">FAQ<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/insurance-claim-glossary/">Claim glossary<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-guides/">Appraisal guides<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></aside></div><section class="band"><div class="wrap band-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email and we’ll talk it through.</p></div><div class="row"><a class="btn btn-white" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-w" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Send the estimate</a></div></div></section>
